<title>USA: CME June live cattle fall sharply in fast trading.</title>
<headline>CME June live cattle fall sharply in fast trading.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME June live cattle futures dropped sharply in fast trading amid rumors cash cattle prices have peaked and may soon trend lower, cattle traders said.</p>
<p>Cash-connected firms were featured sellers in the June, which at one point was down 1.35 cents at 64.050 cents per lb.</p>
<p>At 1059 CDT, live cattle was down 1.050 to 0.250 cent with June off the most at 64.350.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
